      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have some quibbles with the naming. Do we need to talk about splitting and completing connections when all we\u0027re doing is delaying when we accept new connections?\n\nSecondly, couldn\u0027t the `VsockConnectionManager` or its `poll` method take a callback (`on_connection_request`) that receives enough info (e.g. the port) and returns true or false depending on whether to accept the port right away?\n\nConnection requests that are not accepted right away, could go in a separate list (`pending_connections`) and the `VsockConnectionManager` could get a new function (`accept` or `accept_pending`) which accepts one of these and moves it over to `connections`. This ensures that only pending connections can be accepted exactly once. \n\nLMK what you think.",
      "revId": "f41f03cbd723c09ac45ec9b04f7938305b93a681",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
