      "side": 1,
      "message": "The feature is called \"split_accept_connections\" but the operation is called `complete_connection`, not `accept`. Could we avoid talking about completion and just say accept everywhere? Calling this function `accept` would also make the connection to the lower-level API clearer.\n\nI would say that today, connections are automatically accepted. We need a feature to control when connections are accepted. I\u0027m not sure split is the right word there either. Why not `defer_accept`, `wait_to_accept`, `client_accept_connections`, or something along those lines? I don\u0027t know what is best but I would prefer to not introduce new concepts unless we absolutely must.",
